# Pixhawk 6C / ArduPlane — Orin companion on TELEM3 (SERIAL5).
# TELEM1 = DJI, TELEM2 = 3DR. Do not put the Orin on those.
# UART only: TX, RX, GND. Do not feed TELEM3 pin 1 (+5 V) into the Orin.
# Final airframe is a flying wing. The plane that has already flown is a
# normal wing. Companion sends bank + pitch + throttle either way.
# Both surfaces up = nose up. Leave the existing servo directions.
# Cruise is 5–10% throttle at about 100 km/h. Battery in the airframe is 4S.
# Map a rear momentary button to CH7 (Lock) and Switch D to CH8 (Takeover).
# Leave Switch B as the flight-mode switch. It will fight GUIDED if reused.

SERIAL5_PROTOCOL    2
SERIAL5_BAUD        57
SYSID_MYGCS         255

# RC channels and ATTITUDE (yaw) to the companion
SR5_EXTRA1          10
SR5_RCCHAN          10
SR5_POSITION        4
SR5_EXT_STAT        2

# GUIDED attitude from companion. Takeover returns FBWA (mode 5).
# Keep the plane's own LIM_ROLL / LIM_PITCH at least 25° bank,
# 12° nose-up and 10° nose-down. Companion commands stay inside that.
GUID_TIMEOUT        3.0

# Failsafe: radio loss → RTL (plane mode 11). Companion loss is also 3 s.
FS_THR_ENABLE       1
FS_THR_VALUE        975
FS_OPTIONS          0

# CH7/CH8 are companion buttons, not ArduPilot flight-mode functions
RC7_OPTION          0
RC8_OPTION          0
